{"thought": "Casey has not replied, and the calendar copy cannot see January through early March, so there is nothing to offer yet. The ask for windows is carded for Bob's tap, so I'll tell him what it says and what I'm waiting on.", "tool": "tell_bob", "args": {"text": "Casey Lindqvist hasn't replied yet. I took your ask as a 90-minute call on a Meet link sometime in Q1, which I read as January through March. I can't see your calendar for early January through early March yet, so I have no times to offer her.

The card for Approve goes to Casey Lindqvist with you in cc. It introduces me as an assistant agent helping you with scheduling, says you'd like 90 minutes for the annual planning session sometime in Q1, and asks her for a few windows that suit her, with the days and whether morning or afternoon works best. It says I'll check each one against your calendar and come back to her.

Approve sends that note. Once Casey sends windows, I'll check them against your calendar and bring you a time to confirm."}}
